---------------- Known Upstream Intermittent Regression Notes ----------------

The final complete run recorded in this log passed all 5713 tests, with zero
FAILED and zero WRONG results. The notes below do not change that result; they
are provided only to help distinguish known upstream numerical/flaky
regressions from new release blockers in future runs.

1. QS/regtest-kp-1-spg/c_geo_opt_kpsym_spglib.inp

   A protective abort may occur with:
   "No Bloch-phase direction preserves overlap covariance;
   residual=2.8207E-01, irreducible k-point=1, operation=2"

   The CP2K upstream PR #5581 dashboard reported the identical intermittent
   failure. Maintainers concluded that the numerical parameters used to speed
   up the test were too tight and noted that aborting is safer than silently
   producing an incorrect result.

   References:
   https://github.com/cp2k/cp2k/pull/5581#issuecomment-4974228228
   https://github.com/cp2k/cp2k/pull/5581#issuecomment-4978845349

2. QS/regtest-tddfpt-4/test09.inp (TDDFPT_Check_Osc_Strength)

   The current matcher reference is 0.52917241 with a tolerance of 4e-5. One
   observed value was 0.52914924, a relative difference of 4.38e-5, narrowly
   above the threshold. Subsequent isolated, concurrent, and keepalive retests
   all passed. Upstream has relaxed this test's tolerance twice:
   1e-5 -> 2e-5 -> 4e-5.

   References:
   https://github.com/cp2k/cp2k/pull/5213
   https://github.com/cp2k/cp2k/commit/c835e6b7b6995e608e300f0dfa6f0943d2ff96b6

Classification rule: treat a future failure as one of these known upstream
intermittent cases only when both the test name and failure signature match
exactly and a targeted retest passes. Any different test, materially larger
deviation, different residual or signature, or consistently reproducible
failure remains a release blocker.


