Supplemental parallel-matrix validation and known limitations
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
TDDFPT passed all 46/46 checks in each of 8 tested parallel combinations;
relative errors ranged from 5.12e-6 to 1.99e-5, below the 4e-5 tolerance.

SPGLIB passed with 1x1, 1x2, 2x1, 2x2, 1x4, 4x1, 2x4, 8x1, 1x8, and
3x2 decompositions. The 4x2 decomposition failed consistently in 5/5 runs,
with residuals from 0.282 to 0.489; 2x3 and 4x3 also failed. Disabling
keepalive did not resolve the 4x2 failure. With cutoffs increased to 400/60,
4x2 still failed in 1/3 runs.

Conclusion: SPGLIB is sensitive to mixed parallel decomposition and is an
upstream defect candidate. Low cutoffs amplify the issue but are not its sole
root cause. TDDFPT remains tolerance-sensitive numerical variation.